  "version": 1,
  "comment": "Terms for judging a page by its words, used where the domain lists have nothing to say — a new site, a blog post, a marketplace listing, an unclassified search result. Each term sits at the strongest verdict it can support (nsfw / suggestive / immodest) and carries a weight in points; 25 points convicts at that level, and points also count toward every milder level. So one 25-point explicit term is enough on its own, two 12-point terms together are enough, and no amount of swimwear vocabulary can ever add up to 'explicit'. Terms match as whole words only and stop earning points after a few repeats, so a word in a navigation menu cannot convict a page. This is meant to be complete out of the box: an administrator may add or remove a handful, but nobody should have to build it.",
